-## Storage
+## Cookie
 
-Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
+The cookie holds the member and the session's expiry, signed with the key in `LARDER_SESSION_KEY`; `sign` and
+`verify` in `larder/sessions.py` write and check it. A cookie whose signature does not match, or whose expiry has
+passed, logs no one in. Every web server holds the same key, from the deploy secrets, so any server accepts the
+cookie and a deploy logs no one out. Without the variable, larder signs with a development key.
+
+## Known limits
+
+- The server cannot log out one member before their session expires. Workaround: wait out the 30 minutes, or rotate
+  `LARDER_SESSION_KEY`, which logs out every member; rotate it only between pickups.
 
